.TH NETREPORT 1 "2026-09" "mtr-toolbox" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netreport \- one-shot connectivity snapshot for incident notes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netreport
.RI [ host ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints one connectivity snapshot: links, addresses, routes and DNS \(em
and, when given a host, latency and the path to it.
.PP
The output is meant to be pasted into an incident note, so it is a single
run with no options to remember under pressure.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The snapshot was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
A required tool was missing, or the host could not be resolved.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Snapshot this host's networking:
.PP
.RS
.B netreport
.RE
.PP
And the path to a dependency:
.PP
.RS
.B netreport db.internal
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mtr (8),
.BR ip (8),
.BR dig (1).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/mtr-toolbox
.UE
